<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Walk the product — Cybersecurity Assurance</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#fbfcfc;--panel:#fff;--ink:#12201f;--ink2:#3d5250;--ink3:#6d817f;
    --line:#e2e9e8;--line2:#eef3f2;--accent:#0f8f78;--soft:#e6f5f1;--aink:#0a6d5c;
    --crit:#b3261e;--high:#c2410c;--med:#a16207;--low:#0f766e;
    --mono:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;--sans:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"]{
    --bg:#0d1413;--panel:#131c1b;--ink:#e8efee;--ink2:#b3c2c0;--ink3:#829895;
    --line:#243230;--line2:#1b2624;--accent:#3ddfc2;--soft:#12312b;--aink:#6de8d4;
    --crit:#ff8a80;--high:#ffab70;--med:#e8c168;--low:#5ecfba;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:16px;line-height:1.62}
  .shell{display:grid;grid-template-columns:262px minmax(0,1fr)}
  @media(max-width:900px){.shell{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .nav{border-right:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);position:sticky;top:0;height:100vh;overflow-y:auto;padding:22px 16px 60px}
  @media(max-width:900px){.nav{position:static;height:auto;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}}
  .brand{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--aink);font-weight:700}
  .bsub{font-size:17px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.28;margin:6px 0 6px}
  .mirror{font-size:11px;color:var(--ink3);margin-bottom:18px;font-style:italic}
  .grp{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink3);font-weight:700;margin:18px 0 5px;padding-left:9px}
  .nav a{display:block;padding:5px 9px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:6px;color:var(--ink2);text-decoration:none;font-size:13.6px;cursor:pointer;border-left:2px solid transparent}
  .nav a:hover{background:var(--line2);color:var(--ink)}
  .nav a.on{background:var(--soft);color:var(--aink);font-weight:600;border-left-color:var(--accent)}
  .nav a.tab{padding-left:24px;font-size:13px}
  .nav a.dim{opacity:.5}
  .main{padding:46px 44px 120px;max-width:960px}
  @media(max-width:640px){.main{padding:26px 16px 70px}}
  section{display:none}section.on{display:block}
  .crumb{font-size:12px;color:var(--ink3);margin-bottom:10px;font-family:var(--mono)}
  h1{font-size:31px;line-height:1.16;font-weight:660;margin:0 0 12px;letter-spacing:-.02em}
  h2{font-size:20px;font-weight:640;margin:40px 0 12px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  h3{font-size:16px;font-weight:640;margin:26px 0 8px}
  p{margin:0 0 14px;max-width:68ch}
  .lede{font-size:17.5px;color:var(--ink2);max-width:64ch;margin-bottom:24px}
  ul{max-width:66ch;padding-left:22px;margin:0 0 14px}li{margin-bottom:6px}
  code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.87em;background:var(--line2);padding:1.5px 5px;border-radius:4px;color:var(--aink)}
  .fig{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:11px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 8px;overflow-x:auto}
  .cap{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink3);margin:0 0 22px;max-width:64ch}
  .keys{margin:0 0 22px}
  .key{display:flex;gap:12px;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line2)}
  .key:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .kn{flex:0 0 26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-top:1px}
  .kb{flex:1;min-width:0}
  .kt{font-weight:650;font-size:14.6px;margin-bottom:2px}
  .kd{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink2);max-width:62ch}
  .kd .from{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:12.6px;color:var(--ink3)}
  .kd .from b{color:var(--aink);font-weight:650}
  .note{border-left:3px solid var(--accent);background:var(--soft);padding:13px 17px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin:0 0 18px;font-size:14.6px}
  .note.warn{border-left-color:var(--med);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--med) 9%,transparent)}
  .note.bad{border-left-color:var(--crit);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--crit) 9%,transparent)}
  .note p:last-child{margin:0}
  .note .l{display:block;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:5px}
  .biz{border:1px dashed var(--line);border-radius:9px;padding:14px 17px;margin:0 0 18px;background:var(--panel)}
  .biz .l{font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink3);display:block;margin-bottom:5px}
  .tog{position:fixed;top:14px;right:16px;z-index:20;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--ink2);border-radius:7px;padding:6px 11px;font-size:12.5px;cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit}
  .tog:focus-visible,.nav a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
  .wrap{overflow-x:auto;margin:0 0 18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px}
  table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;min-width:460px}
  th{text-align:left;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink3);font-weight:700;padding:9px 12px;background:var(--line2);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  td{padding:9px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line2);vertical-align:top}
  tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}
  svg text{font-family:var(--sans)}
  .foot{color:var(--ink3);font-size:13.4px;margin-top:44px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .foot a{color:var(--aink)}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<button class="tog" id="tt">Theme</button>
<div class="shell">

<nav class="nav">
  <div class="brand">Compliverse</div>
  <div class="bsub">Walk the product</div>
  <div class="mirror">This sidebar mirrors the app's own</div>

  <div class="grp">Cybersecurity Assurance</div>
  <a data-go="p-assets" class="on">IT Assets</a>
  <a data-go="p-asset-detail" class="tab">↳ Asset detail</a>
  <a data-go="p-rp">Risk Posture</a>
  <a data-go="p-rp-asset" class="tab">↳ Asset posture</a>
  <a data-go="p-vulns">Vulnerabilities</a>
  <a data-go="p-vuln-detail" class="tab">↳ Finding detail</a>

  <div class="grp">Also in this module</div>
  <a data-go="p-more">Discovery · Criticality</a>

  <div class="grp">Reference</div>
  <a data-go="p-index">Full field guide →</a>
</nav>

<main class="main">

<!-- ══════ IT ASSETS ══════ -->
<section id="p-assets" class="on">
  <div class="crumb">Sidebar → Cybersecurity Assurance → IT Assets</div>
  <h1>IT Assets</h1>
  <p class="lede">The register of everything you own. Every score in the module ultimately hangs off a row in this list.</p>

  <div class="fig">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 300" width="100%" height="300" role="img" aria-label="Annotated asset register list">
      <rect x="10" y="10" width="820" height="46" rx="8" fill="var(--line2)"/>
      <text x="28" y="32" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">IT Asset Inventory</text>
      <text x="28" y="48" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">15 assets</text>
      <rect x="700" y="22" width="112" height="24" rx="6" fill="var(--accent)" opacity=".9"/>
      <text x="756" y="38" font-size="12" font-weight="650" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">+ Add asset</text>

      <rect x="10" y="66" width="820" height="30" rx="5" fill="var(--line2)" opacity=".7"/>
      <g font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".7">
        <text x="30" y="86">NAME</text><text x="290" y="86">TYPE</text><text x="400" y="86">CRITICALITY</text>
        <text x="540" y="86">OWNER</text><text x="670" y="86">RISK</text><text x="750" y="86">FINDINGS</text>
      </g>

      <g font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="10" y="100" width="820" height="42" fill="var(--panel)"/>
        <text x="30" y="126" font-weight="600">nw-vpn01</text><text x="290" y="126" opacity=".7">infrastructure</text>
        <rect x="400" y="112" width="58" height="20" rx="10" fill="var(--crit)" opacity=".16"/><text x="429" y="126" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--crit)" font-weight="650">critical</text>
        <text x="540" y="126" opacity=".7">L. Wei</text><text x="670" y="126" font-weight="700" fill="var(--crit)">86</text><text x="762" y="126" opacity=".8">4</text>

        <rect x="10" y="144" width="820" height="42" fill="var(--panel)"/>
        <line x1="10" y1="144" x2="830" y2="144" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="30" y="170" font-weight="600">[DEMO] Asset 06</text><text x="290" y="170" opacity=".7">server</text>
        <rect x="400" y="156" width="48" height="20" rx="10" fill="var(--high)" opacity=".16"/><text x="424" y="170" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--high)" font-weight="650">high</text>
        <text x="540" y="170" opacity=".7">Unassigned</text><text x="670" y="170" font-weight="700" fill="var(--med)">41</text><text x="762" y="170" opacity=".8">1</text>

        <rect x="10" y="188" width="820" height="42" fill="var(--panel)"/>
        <line x1="10" y1="188" x2="830" y2="188" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="30" y="214" font-weight="600">Windows MSRPC @ 127.0.0.1</text><text x="290" y="214" opacity=".7">application</text>
        <rect x="400" y="200" width="62" height="20" rx="10" fill="var(--med)" opacity=".16"/><text x="431" y="214" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--med)" font-weight="650">medium</text>
        <text x="540" y="214" opacity=".7">Unassigned</text><text x="670" y="214" font-weight="700" fill="var(--med)">35</text><text x="762" y="214" opacity=".8">1</text>
      </g>
      <line x1="10" y1="232" x2="830" y2="232" stroke="var(--line)"/>

      <!-- callouts -->
      <g>
        <circle cx="150" cy="121" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="150" y="126" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">1</text>
        <circle cx="429" cy="255" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="429" y="260" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">2</text>
        <line x1="429" y1="242" x2="429" y2="180" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="680" cy="255" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="680" y="260" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">3</text>
        <line x1="680" y1="242" x2="676" y2="180" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="768" cy="255" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="768" y="260" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">4</text>
        <line x1="768" y1="242" x2="764" y2="180" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="cap">The register. Click any row to open its detail page.</p>

  <div class="keys">
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">1</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Asset name</div><div class="kd">Identity. An "@ address" suffix means this asset was <em>promoted from detected software</em> — an application running on a host, given its own record.<span class="from">From: <b>manual entry</b>, CSV import, agent discovery, or software promotion</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">2</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Criticality</div><div class="kd">The most consequential field in the module. It feeds vulnerability priority (10% of it), the CIA dimension of posture, and one of the six remediation triggers.<span class="from">From: <b>derived from C/I/A ratings</b>, or a formal criticality assessment</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">3</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Risk score</div><div class="kd">The composite posture score, 0–100, higher is worse. Identical to the number on the Risk Posture page — one asset, one risk number.<span class="from">From: <b>the risk posture engine</b>, five weighted dimensions</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">4</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Findings</div><div class="kd">Count of <em>open</em> vulnerabilities. Remediated, verified, closed, resolved and accepted findings are excluded — closing one drops this number.<span class="from">From: <b>linked vulnerabilities</b>, filtered by status</span></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="biz">
    <span class="l">Why this page comes first</span>
    <p>You cannot rank risk on things you have not listed. Every other screen in this module is a view <em>through</em> an asset — a vulnerability with no asset is an abstract fact about software, not a risk to your business.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ ASSET DETAIL ══════ -->
<section id="p-asset-detail">
  <div class="crumb">IT Assets → [DEMO] Asset 06</div>
  <h1>Asset detail</h1>
  <p class="lede">Twelve tabs, grouped into five questions. Everything known about one machine.</p>

  <div class="fig">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 330" width="100%" height="330" role="img" aria-label="Annotated asset detail page with tab bar">
      <rect x="10" y="10" width="820" height="52" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/>
      <text x="30" y="34" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">[DEMO] Asset 06</text>
      <text x="30" y="52" font-size="11.5" font-family="var(--mono)" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">server · high criticality · not internet-facing</text>

      <!-- tab bar -->
      <rect x="10" y="72" width="820" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--line2)"/>
      <g font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="16" y="77" width="68" height="24" rx="5" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--accent)"/><text x="50" y="93" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" fill="var(--aink)">Overview</text>
        <text x="118" y="93" opacity=".72">Risk &amp; Controls</text>
        <text x="222" y="93" opacity=".72">Vulnerabilities</text>
        <text x="318" y="93" opacity=".72">Software</text>
        <text x="386" y="93" opacity=".72">Relationships</text>
        <text x="482" y="93" opacity=".72">Lifecycle</text>
        <text x="546" y="93" opacity=".72">Compliance</text>
        <text x="626" y="93" opacity=".72">Trajectory</text>
        <text x="700" y="93" opacity=".72">Criticality</text>
        <text x="774" y="93" opacity=".72">Notes</text>
      </g>

      <!-- stat strip -->
      <rect x="10" y="118" width="820" height="72" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/>
      <g fill="currentColor">
        <text x="42" y="142" font-size="10" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8">RISK SCORE</text>
        <text x="42" y="172" font-size="24" font-weight="700" fill="var(--med)">41</text>
        <line x1="174" y1="128" x2="174" y2="180" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="204" y="142" font-size="10" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8">OPEN FINDINGS</text>
        <text x="204" y="172" font-size="24" font-weight="700">1</text>
        <line x1="338" y1="128" x2="338" y2="180" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="368" y="142" font-size="10" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8">BLAST RADIUS</text>
        <text x="368" y="172" font-size="24" font-weight="700">0</text>
        <line x1="502" y1="128" x2="502" y2="180" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="532" y="142" font-size="10" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8">CONTROL COVERAGE</text>
        <text x="532" y="172" font-size="24" font-weight="700">0%</text>
        <line x1="676" y1="128" x2="676" y2="180" stroke="var(--line)"/>
        <text x="706" y="142" font-size="10" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8">REFRESH DUE</text>
        <text x="706" y="172" font-size="24" font-weight="700" opacity=".45">—</text>
      </g>

      <!-- group brackets under tabs -->
      <g stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none" opacity=".7">
        <path d="M16,212 L16,222 L300,222 L300,212"/>
        <path d="M318,212 L318,222 L466,222 L466,212"/>
        <path d="M482,212 L482,222 L610,222 L610,212"/>
        <path d="M626,212 L626,222 L686,222 L686,212"/>
        <path d="M700,212 L700,222 L820,222 L820,212"/>
      </g>
      <g font-size="11" fill="var(--aink)" font-weight="650" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="158" y="240">what is wrong with it</text>
        <text x="392" y="240">how it connects</text>
        <text x="546" y="240">how it's protected</text>
        <text x="656" y="240">the chain</text>
        <text x="760" y="240">the record</text>
      </g>

      <g>
        <circle cx="50" cy="272" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="50" y="277" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">1</text>
        <line x1="50" y1="259" x2="50" y2="108" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="368" cy="272" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="368" y="277" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">2</text>
        <line x1="368" y1="259" x2="368" y2="190" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
        <circle cx="532" cy="272" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="532" y="277" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">3</text>
        <line x1="532" y1="259" x2="532" y2="190" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      </g>
      <text x="20" y="312" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">Tabs group into five questions — that grouping is the page's structure, not decoration.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="cap">Overview tab shown. The five bracketed groups are how the twelve tabs are meant to be read.</p>

  <div class="keys">
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">1</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Overview tab — identity and the five headline numbers</div><div class="kd">Ownership, network, hardware, procurement. It also absorbed the old Discovery and Assignments tabs, whose fields already lived here.<span class="from">From: <b>the asset record</b> plus the posture engine for the score</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">2</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Blast radius = 0</div><div class="kd"><strong>Unmapped, not contained.</strong> No relationship has been declared and nothing shares its address. Declare dependencies on the Relationships tab and this fills in.<span class="from">From: <b>declared relationships</b> + assets sharing a routable IP (loopback excluded)</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">3</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Control coverage = 0%</div><div class="kd">Zero of a target of twelve controls linked. This same percentage appears on Risk &amp; Controls and drives 15% of the posture score — one formula, three places.<span class="from">From: <b>control links ÷ 12</b></span></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="note warn">
    <span class="l">Reading empty numbers correctly</span>
    <p>Blast radius 0 and coverage 0% both mean <em>nobody has recorded this yet</em>. They are not evidence of isolation or of a control gap being closed. Absence of data and a good result look identical if you only read the number.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ RISK POSTURE ══════ -->
<section id="p-rp">
  <div class="crumb">Sidebar → Cybersecurity Assurance → Risk Posture</div>
  <h1>Risk Posture</h1>
  <p class="lede">The portfolio view: one score per asset, ranked, with a band distribution.</p>

  <div class="fig">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 260" width="100%" height="260" role="img" aria-label="Risk posture dashboard with gauge and band distribution">
      <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="58" fill="none" stroke="var(--line2)" stroke-width="14"/>
      <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="58" fill="none" stroke="var(--med)" stroke-width="14"
              stroke-dasharray="120 245" stroke-linecap="round" transform="rotate(-90 110 110)"/>
      <text x="110" y="106" font-size="30" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--med)">33</text>
      <text x="110" y="126" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">avg risk /100</text>
      <text x="110" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity=".7">15 of 15 assets scored</text>

      <g font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="220" y="46" width="140" height="62" rx="8" fill="var(--low)" opacity=".14"/>
        <text x="290" y="76" font-size="24" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--low)">5</text>
        <text x="290" y="95" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--low)" font-weight="650">CONTAINED</text>

        <rect x="372" y="46" width="140" height="62" rx="8" fill="var(--med)" opacity=".16"/>
        <text x="442" y="76" font-size="24" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--med)">8</text>
        <text x="442" y="95" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--med)" font-weight="650">WATCH</text>

        <rect x="524" y="46" width="140" height="62" rx="8" fill="var(--high)" opacity=".16"/>
        <text x="594" y="76" font-size="24" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--high)">2</text>
        <text x="594" y="95" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--high)" font-weight="650">ELEVATED</text>

        <rect x="676" y="46" width="140" height="62" rx="8" fill="var(--crit)" opacity=".14"/>
        <text x="746" y="76" font-size="24" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--crit)">0</text>
        <text x="746" y="95" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--crit)" font-weight="650">SEVERE</text>
      </g>

      <rect x="220" y="126" width="596" height="1" fill="var(--line)"/>
      <text x="220" y="150" font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".72">Highest risk: <tspan font-weight="700">nw-vpn01</tspan> — 86/100</text>

      <circle cx="110" cy="222" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="110" y="227" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">1</text>
      <line x1="110" y1="209" x2="110" y2="176" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <circle cx="442" cy="222" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="442" y="227" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">2</text>
      <line x1="442" y1="209" x2="442" y2="112" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="cap">Clicking a band filters the list below it.</p>

  <div class="keys">
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">1</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Portfolio average</div><div class="kd">Mean score across scored assets. Reads <strong>—</strong>, not 0, when nothing has been scored — because "we measured nothing" and "everything is perfect" must not look the same.<span class="from">From: <b>the posture engine</b>, averaged</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">2</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Bands</div><div class="kd">contained 0–25 · watch 25–50 · elevated 50–75 · severe 75–100. Deliberately different words from asset <em>criticality</em> (low/medium/high/critical), so "a high asset with high risk" can't happen.<span class="from">From: <b>score thresholds</b></span></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ RP ASSET ══════ -->
<section id="p-rp-asset">
  <div class="crumb">Risk Posture → Windows MSRPC @ 127.0.0.1</div>
  <h1>Asset posture detail</h1>
  <p class="lede">The score, broken into its five dimensions — and the confidence behind it.</p>

  <div class="fig">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 250" width="100%" height="250" role="img" aria-label="Score breakdown bar with excluded dimensions">
      <text x="20" y="30" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">Score breakdown</text>
      <rect x="20" y="44" width="796" height="26" rx="5" fill="var(--line2)"/>
      <rect x="20" y="44" width="418" height="26" rx="5" fill="var(--high)" opacity=".85"/>
      <text x="229" y="62" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">18.3</text>
      <rect x="440" y="44" width="380" height="26" fill="#a78bfa" opacity=".85"/>
      <text x="630" y="62" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">16.7</text>

      <g font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor">
        <text x="20" y="96" opacity=".38">■ CIS gap (25% muted) → 0 pts · no data, excluded</text>
        <text x="20" y="118" fill="var(--high)" font-weight="650">■ Vulnerabilities (67%) → 18.3 pts</text>
        <text x="20" y="140" fill="#8b5cf6" font-weight="650">■ CIA value (33%) → 16.7 pts</text>
        <text x="20" y="162" opacity=".38">■ Control gap (15% muted) → 0 pts · no data, excluded</text>
        <text x="20" y="184" opacity=".38">■ Linked risks (15% muted) → 0 pts · no data, excluded</text>
      </g>

      <rect x="470" y="86" width="346" height="104" rx="8" fill="var(--med)" opacity=".1"/>
      <text x="490" y="110" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="var(--med)">Data quality 45%</text>
      <text x="490" y="132" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity=".75">Two of five dimensions have evidence.</text>
      <text x="490" y="150" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity=".75">The other three are excluded, and the two</text>
      <text x="490" y="168" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity=".75">that remain carry 100% between them.</text>

      <circle cx="36" cy="220" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="36" y="225" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">1</text>
      <line x1="36" y1="207" x2="36" y2="126" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <circle cx="200" cy="220" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="200" y="225" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">2</text>
      <line x1="200" y1="207" x2="200" y2="168" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <circle cx="640" cy="220" r="13" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="640" y="225" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">3</text>
      <line x1="640" y1="207" x2="640" y2="192" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="cap">The same asset shown earlier — 34.9/100, with three dimensions excluded.</p>

  <div class="keys">
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">1</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">The percentage is the <em>effective</em> share</div><div class="kd">Vulnerabilities is weighted 30% by default — but with three dimensions excluded it carries <strong>67%</strong> of this asset's score. Showing the raw 30% beside 18.3 pts made the legend look like broken arithmetic.<span class="from">From: <b>weight ÷ sum of known weights</b></span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">2</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">"no data, excluded"</div><div class="kd">Zero points here means <strong>unknown</strong>, not "no gap". Without that label, "Control gap → 0 pts" reads as good news when it means nothing has been measured.<span class="from">From: <b>the known flag</b> on each dimension</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">3</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Data quality</div><div class="kd">The share of scoring weight actually backed by evidence. <strong>Read it with the score, never alone.</strong> A low score at 45% quality is a much weaker claim than the same score at 95%.<span class="from">From: <b>sum of known weights</b></span></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="note bad">
    <span class="l">The single most common misreading</span>
    <p>A new asset with nothing recorded shows a low score and a reassuring green band, because it is judged on one or two dimensions. <strong>That is "we don't know", not "it's fine."</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ VULNS ══════ -->
<section id="p-vulns">
  <div class="crumb">Sidebar → Cybersecurity Assurance → Vulnerabilities</div>
  <h1>Vulnerabilities</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every finding across the estate, ranked. This is the work queue.</p>

  <div class="wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Means</th><th>Comes from</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Severity</strong></td><td>How bad the flaw is <em>in general</em></td><td>CVSS, from NVD</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Priority</strong></td><td>How urgent it is <em>for you</em>, 0–100</td><td>Our 7-signal engine</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Status</strong></td><td>open → in progress → remediated → verified</td><td>Your workflow</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Due date</strong></td><td>Deadline by severity</td><td>Your SLA policy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>KEV / exploit chips</strong></td><td>Threat flags at a glance</td><td>CISA, GitHub</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <div class="note warn">
    <span class="l">Sort by priority, not severity</span>
    <p>A CVSS 9.8 with no published exploit, on an internal box, behind a patch you already applied, is not your most urgent problem. Severity describes the flaw; priority describes your exposure to it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="biz">
    <span class="l">What "EPSS" means when you see it here</span>
    <p>EPSS ships <strong>two</strong> numbers from FIRST: the <em>probability</em> of exploitation in the next 30 days (0.5% means 0.5%), and the <em>percentile</em> (37th means it ranks above 37% of all CVEs). They are not interchangeable — reading a percentile as a probability overstates risk by roughly seventy times.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ VULN DETAIL ══════ -->
<section id="p-vuln-detail">
  <div class="crumb">Vulnerabilities → VULN-37 · CVE-2024-2005</div>
  <h1>Finding detail</h1>
  <p class="lede">Five tabs, each answering one question. In order: what is it, what do we do, could it be used, what happened, what did people say.</p>

  <div class="fig">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 210" width="100%" height="210" role="img" aria-label="Vulnerability detail tabs and their questions">
      <rect x="10" y="14" width="820" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--line2)"/>
      <g font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="18" y="20" width="74" height="24" rx="5" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--accent)"/><text x="55" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" fill="var(--aink)">Analysis</text>
        <text x="132" y="36" opacity=".72">Remediation</text>
        <text x="238" y="36" opacity=".72">Exploit Test</text>
        <text x="342" y="36" opacity=".72">History</text>
        <text x="416" y="36" opacity=".72">Notes</text>
      </g>
      <g font-size="11.5" fill="var(--aink)" font-weight="600">
        <text x="55" y="76" text-anchor="middle">how bad?</text>
        <text x="168" y="76" text-anchor="middle">what do we do?</text>
        <text x="272" y="76" text-anchor="middle">could it be used?</text>
        <text x="362" y="76" text-anchor="middle">what happened?</text>
        <text x="432" y="76" text-anchor="middle">who said what?</text>
      </g>

      <rect x="10" y="98" width="400" height="96" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/>
      <text x="30" y="122" font-size="11" font-weight="700" opacity=".55" letter-spacing=".8" fill="currentColor">RISK SCORE</text>
      <text x="30" y="158" font-size="30" font-weight="700" fill="var(--med)">41</text>
      <text x="76" y="158" font-size="13" fill="currentColor" opacity=".55">/ 100</text>
      <text x="30" y="180" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">CVSS 7.1 · EPSS 0.5% · not in KEV · 256 exploits</text>

      <rect x="424" y="98" width="406" height="96" rx="8" fill="var(--crit)" opacity=".08"/>
      <text x="444" y="122" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="var(--crit)" letter-spacing=".8">WHY THIS NEEDS ACTION NOW</text>
      <text x="444" y="146" font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".8">• Public exploit code is published</text>
      <text x="444" y="168" font-size="12.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".8">• 1 day past its due date</text>

      <circle cx="446" cy="80" r="12" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="446" y="85" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff">1</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="keys">
    <div class="key"><div class="kn">1</div><div class="kb"><div class="kt">Red flags — what actually starts the work</div><div class="kd">The score <em>ranks</em> the queue. These flags decide it needs action <em>today</em>. Six exist: CISA KEV, any public exploit, EPSS ≥ 10%, past due date, internet-facing asset, business-critical asset. <strong>An empty list is a real answer</strong> — the finding waits for the normal patch cycle.<span class="from">From: <b>raw facts checked individually</b>, never the blended score</span></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Tab</th><th>What it holds</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Analysis</strong></td><td>The score with its 7-signal breakdown, threat narrative, and the controls this finding breaks. Diagnoses; never proposes fixes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Remediation</strong></td><td>Three groups: the fix (plan + lifecycle + patch availability) · who owns it · if we're not fixing it yet (mitigations + exception).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Exploit Test</strong></td><td>Can it be reached (MITRE kill chain + evidence) · how far would it spread · prove it (retest log). Nothing is executed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>History</strong></td><td>Every state change with actor and timestamp. The tab an auditor opens first.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Notes</strong></td><td>Human reasoning that must outlive a status field.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ MORE ══════ -->
<section id="p-more">
  <div class="crumb">Sidebar → Cybersecurity Assurance</div>
  <h1>The rest of the module</h1>
  <p class="lede">Same pattern, briefer treatment.</p>

  <h3>Asset Discovery</h3>
  <p>Where assets arrive from before anyone curates them. Agent and scan results land here and are promoted into the register. Carries <code>last_seen_at</code>, which is how you tell a live estate from a stale one.</p>

  <h3>Criticality Assessments</h3>
  <p>The formal, reviewed version of "how much does this matter" — ISCA rates the system, IACA rates the data it holds. Each produces a score, a band and an approval status.</p>
  <div class="note warn">
    <span class="l">Known gap</span>
    <p>The formal assessment and the criticality derived from C/I/A ratings do not reconcile. The scoring engine uses the derived value. Where they disagree, nothing currently flags it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="foot">
    This walkthrough follows the product's own navigation. For field-by-field depth — every scoring weight, every data source, the full glossary — see the <a href="/guide">full field guide</a>.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════ INDEX ══════ -->
<section id="p-index">
  <div class="crumb">Reference</div>
  <h1>Full field guide</h1>
  <p class="lede">This walkthrough is the guided tour. The field guide is the reference.</p>
  <p>It covers every tab in depth, the complete scoring model with worked examples, the exploit and weaponised logic, all data sources, a glossary, and an honest list of limitations.</p>
  <p style="font-size:17px"><a href="/guide" style="color:var(--aink);font-weight:650">Open the full field guide →</a></p>
  <div class="foot">Both documents ship with the product. <code>/guide</code> to read, <code>/guide/walkthrough.html</code> to present.</div>
</section>

</main>
</div>
<script>
  var links=document.querySelectorAll('.nav a[data-go]'),secs=document.querySelectorAll('main section');
  function go(id){
    secs.forEach(function(s){s.classList.toggle('on',s.id===id)});
    links.forEach(function(a){a.classList.toggle('on',a.dataset.go===id)});
    window.scrollTo(0,0);
  }
  links.forEach(function(a){a.addEventListener('click',function(e){e.preventDefault();go(a.dataset.go)})});
  var root=document.documentElement;
  if(window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)root.setAttribute('data-theme','dark');
  document.getElementById('tt').addEventListener('click',function(){
    root.setAttribute('data-theme',root.getAttribute('data-theme')==='dark'?'light':'dark');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
